  "scope_limits": [
    "E plus global allocator meter is an independent instrumented diagnostic ELF; all its CPU/latency observations are EXCLUDED.",
    "Cached-step accounting includes receive/admission/process_udp/send and owned drops; actual cached classification counts include real cache hits during prewarm. No hardcoded5000 denominator.",
    "Whole-owner-turn categories include normal wait/control and upstream completion work. no_packet means no classified incoming UDP request in that turn, not necessarily idle work or an EAGAIN syscall.",
    "Cached-only turn averages are conditional on that class. All-turn totals also include cache fill, upstream completions and other work; they are reported separately.",
    "Owner-loop counts exclude initialization before the loop, report formatting and later teardown. All-turn totals are not whole-process-lifetime allocation/leak accounting.",
    "Allocation bytes are successful allocator requests/releases, not physical allocator footprint/RSS/USS. Realloc counts are separate.",
    "Observed totals match the earlier local API-subset count numerically, but this alone does not attribute each allocation site or prove uninstrumented artifact cost. No C allocation comparison or speedup is inferred."
